      <h1 class="hero-title">Pace</h1>
      <p class="hero-supertitle">
        AI specialists for every role at your company.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">
        Sales prep their calls. Engineers review their PRs. Finance closes the month. Marketing ships campaigns. Each role gets Claude with the right skills loaded, connected to the tools they actually use, tuned to how your team works.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta-row">
        <a href="/docs/install" class="cta cta-primary">Get started</a>
        <a href="mailto:hello@goldenberry.so" class="cta cta-secondary">Talk to us</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-proof" aria-label="Works with" data-reveal>
      <span class="hero-proof-label">Works with</span>
      <ul class="hero-proof-list" role="list">
        <li>Claude Code</li>
        <li>Cursor</li>
        <li>Gemini CLI</li>
        <li>Codex CLI</li>
        <li>VS Code Copilot</li>
        <li>Kiro</li>
        <li>OpenCode</li>
        <li>RovoDev</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================
       INSTALL PATHS, two-up below the hero
       ============================================ -->
  <section class="section install-paths" id="install-paths" aria-label="Install paths">
    <div class="install-paths-inner" data-reveal-stagger>
      <div class="install-card install-card-cowork">
        <span class="install-card-label">Click to install</span>
        <h3>Cowork (desktop)</h3>
        <p>One link per plugin. Cowork opens and asks you to confirm. Pick the team you're on:</p>
        <ul class="install-quicklinks" role="list">
          <li><a class="install-quicklink" href="https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&plugin=sales" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Install sales</span><span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a></li>
          <li><a class="install-quicklink" href="https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&plugin=marketing" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Install marketing</span><span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a></li>
          <li><a class="install-quicklink" href="https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&plugin=engineering" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Install engineering</span><span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a></li>
          <li><a class="install-quicklink" href="https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&plugin=data" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Install data</span><span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a></li>
          <li><a class="install-quicklink" href="https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&plugin=finance" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Install finance</span><span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a></li>
          <li><a class="install-quicklink" href="https://claude.ai/desktop/customize/plugins/new?marketplace=GoldenBerry-SO/Pace&plugin=product-management" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Install product</span><span aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</span></a></li>
        </ul>
        <a class="install-card-cta" href="/plugins">See all 50 plugins &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="install-card install-card-terminal">
        <span class="install-card-label">Run in terminal</span>
        <h3>Claude Code (CLI)</h3>
        <p>Three lines and you're in. Replace <code>sales</code> with whichever team you're on.</p>
        <div class="install-terminal">
          <pre class="terminal-body"><code><span class="prompt">$</span> claude plugin marketplace add GoldenBerry-SO/Pace
<span class="muted">Registers 50 plugins.</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> claude plugin install sales@pace
<span class="prompt">&gt;</span> Prep me for the Acme call.</code></pre>
        </div>
        <a class="install-card-cta" href="/docs/install#claude-code">Full install docs &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================
       WHO'S IT FOR, persona shortcuts
       ============================================ -->
  <section class="section roles" id="roles" aria-labelledby="roles-title">
    <div class="roles-inner">
      <div class="roles-head" data-reveal>
        <span class="roles-eyebrow">Who's it for</span>
        <h2 class="roles-title" id="roles-title">Pick the team you're on.</h2>
        <p class="roles-lede">
          Every role gets a starter set: the plugins to install, the workflows that fit a typical week, and one-click install in Cowork. Click your team to see the brief.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="roles-grid" role="list" data-reveal-stagger>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/sales"><span class="role-card-name">Sales</span><span class="role-card-blurb">Prep calls, run pipeline reviews, draft outreach.</span></a></li>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/marketing"><span class="role-card-name">Marketing</span><span class="role-card-blurb">Plan campaigns, draft content, enforce brand voice.</span></a></li>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/engineering"><span class="role-card-name">Engineering</span><span class="role-card-blurb">Stacked-PR shipping, code review, diagnosis, TDD.</span></a></li>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/data"><span class="role-card-name">Data</span><span class="role-card-blurb">SQL drafting, anomaly digests, dashboards.</span></a></li>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/product"><span class="role-card-name">Product</span><span class="role-card-blurb">User-research synthesis, specs, competitive briefs.</span></a></li>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/finance"><span class="role-card-name">Finance</span><span class="role-card-blurb">Month-end runbook, variance, journal entries.</span></a></li>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/legal"><span class="role-card-name">Legal</span><span class="role-card-blurb">NDA triage, contract review, compliance.</span></a></li>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/operations"><span class="role-card-name">Operations</span><span class="role-card-blurb">Cross-team digests, vendor review, runbooks.</span></a></li>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/people"><span class="role-card-name">People</span><span class="role-card-blurb">Recruiting pipeline, interview prep, offer letters.</span></a></li>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/customer-support"><span class="role-card-name">Customer Support</span><span class="role-card-blurb">Ticket triage, response drafts, escalation.</span></a></li>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/productivity"><span class="role-card-name">Productivity</span><span class="role-card-blurb">Task management, daily updates, project memory.</span></a></li>
        <li><a class="role-card" href="/docs/teams/design"><span class="role-card-name">Design</span><span class="role-card-blurb">Defers to impeccable for frontend craft.</span></a></li>
      </ul>


    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================
       ENGINEERING DEEP-LINK
       ============================================ -->
  <section class="section eng-band" id="for-engineering" aria-label="Pace for engineering" data-reveal>
    <div class="eng-band-inner">
      <div class="eng-band-left">
        <span class="eng-band-eyebrow">For engineering</span>
        <h2 class="eng-band-title">A disciplined toolkit for shipping software.</h2>
        <p class="eng-band-lede">
          Engineers get 34 engineering skills covering the full week: a stacked-PR workflow that gives shipping a shape (<code>spec</code> &rarr; <code>implement</code> &rarr; <code>review</code> &rarr; <code>topr</code> &rarr; <code>next</code>), plus careful-review, TDD, diagnose, security-review, and the rest.
        </p>
        <div class="eng-band-row">
          <a class="cta cta-primary" href="/for-engineering">Pace for engineering</a>
          <a class="cta cta-secondary" href="/cookbook/engineering">Engineering cookbook</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="eng-band-right" aria-hidden="true">
        <ul class="eng-band-skills" role="list">
          <li><code>spec</code></li>
          <li><code>implement</code></li>
          <li><code>review</code></li>
          <li><code>topr</code></li>
          <li><code>next</code></li>
          <li><code>grill-me</code></li>
          <li><code>tdd</code></li>
          <li><code>careful-review</code></li>
          <li><code>find-missing-tests</code></li>
          <li><code>diagnose</code></li>
          <li><code>debug</code></li>
          <li><code>security-review</code></li>
          <li><code>e2e-test</code></li>
          <li><code>codex-review</code></li>
          <li><code>ship-pr</code></li>
          <li><code>prototype</code></li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================
       01. THE FOUNDATION
       ============================================ -->
  <section class="section foundation" id="foundation">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <span class="section-number">01</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">The Foundation</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p class="section-lede">
        Three layers stacked on Claude: a plugin per role, MCP connectors to the tools your team already uses, and the /pace router on top for the commands that match how your team actually works.
      </p>

      <div class="foundation-grid" data-reveal-stagger>
        <article class="foundation-card">
          <h3>Skills for every role</h3>
          <p>A plugin per department: sales, marketing, finance, legal, engineering, data, customer support, product, HR, ops, design. Install only what your team uses. Each plugin's skills auto-trigger when the work matches.</p>
          <span class="foundation-card-status">50 plugins</span>
        </article>
        <article class="foundation-card">
          <h3>Connected to your stack</h3>
          <p>Plugins talk to Slack, HubSpot, Snowflake, Notion, Linear, and the rest through MCP. Claude reads your actual data and writes back to your actual tools, not invented examples.</p>
          <span class="foundation-card-status">Your tools</span>
        </article>
        <article class="foundation-card">
          <h3>Your team's way</h3>
          <p>The <code>/pace</code> router sits on top. Codify how <em>your</em> team ships, reviews, onboards, and operates. Sub-commands grow as your playbook crystallizes.</p>
          <span class="foundation-card-status">Custom</span>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="foundation-cta">
        <p>
          Register the marketplace once, then install the plugins your team actually uses. <a href="#downloads" class="text-link">See get started &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================
       02. THE LANGUAGE
       ============================================ -->
  <section class="section language" id="language">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <span class="section-number">02</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">The Catalog</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p class="section-lede">
        Fifty plugins. Each one is scoped to a single role; install only what your team uses. The <code>/pace</code> router on top is for your team's own commands.
      </p>

      <div class="catalog-grid">
        <a class="catalog-card catalog-card-router" href="/plugins/pace">
          <div class="catalog-card-meta">
            <span class="catalog-card-prefix">/pace</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-tag">Router</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Your team's commands</h3>
          <p>Codify how your team ships, reviews, onboards, and operates. <code>/pace teach</code> sets up project context once. Build commands as your playbook crystallizes.</p>
          <span class="catalog-card-author">Custom</span>
        </a>

        <a class="catalog-card" href="/plugins/sales">
          <div class="catalog-card-meta">
            <span class="catalog-card-prefix">/sales:*</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-tag">9 workflows</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Sales</h3>
          <p>Prospect, prep calls, manage pipeline, draft outreach, build battlecards.</p>
          <span class="catalog-card-author">Anthropic</span>
        </a>

        <a class="catalog-card" href="/plugins/marketing">
          <div class="catalog-card-meta">
            <span class="catalog-card-prefix">/marketing:*</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-tag">8 workflows</span>
          </div>
